    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead">Columbia University <lb/>in the City of
                            <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>
                        <lb/>[<rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">NEW YORK</rs> 27, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N. Y.</rs>] <lb/>OFFICE OF THE
                        CHAPLAIN</fw><fw place="left" type="adressline">The Reverend <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul J. Tillich</rs>, Ph.
                        D. <lb/>Union Theological Seminary <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319"
                            type="place">New York City</rs></fw>
                    <dateline><date when="1946-08-08">August 8, 1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I hope you know how tremendously gratified and moved we all were last Sunday at
                    your magnificent sermon. You were good enough to tell me that the sermon had a
                    certain personal bearing. Perhaps knowing that quickened my feelings about it a
                    little. I must tell you that it has been many a long day since there have been
                    said in Chapel such great and simple statements of fact. I don&apos;t suppose we
                    shall hear them soon again I was myself much moved by what you said, because you
                    seemed so clearly to be talking about myself and to have penetrated to a region
                    in which I am not yet at home. Many, many thanks.</p>
                <p>I hope you will not forget to let me have a copy of your manuscript, if that is
                    convenient to you. I don&apos;t know what other plans you may have, but I should
                    like at least the privilege of having it mimeographed and sent out to some in
                    the Chapel family who would especially appreciate reading it.</p>

                <closer><salute>With warm thanks again and best wishes for your birthday, believe
                        me</salute><signed>Yours very sincerely, <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__162"
                            type="person">Stephen F. Bayne, Jr.</rs><lb/>Chaplain</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
